// Signing. This file IS versioned and is the one the .xcodeproj references:
// Xcode refuses to open a project whose base configuration does not exist, so
// the one that may be missing is not this one but the one it includes.
//
// `#include?` (with the question mark) is an OPTIONAL xcconfig include: if
// Local.xcconfig is not there, it is silently ignored and the app builds for
// the simulator with no team. If it is there, what it says overrides this.
//
// What each person puts in Local.xcconfig (team, identity, profile) is not
// written here nor in project.yml, because `xcodegen generate` regenerates the
// .xcodeproj and whatever is set by hand in Signing & Capabilities is lost.
// See Local.xcconfig.example.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
